WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.900
Sometimes we wait to feel confident before we begin.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.767
But confidence can develop through practice—even when the first attempt feels

3
00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:12.300
awkward.

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.709
The starting point doesn’t need to be impressive. It needs to be manageable.

5
00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:24.544
‘Be more confident around people’ is a big goal. It doesn’t tell you what to

6
00:00:24.544 --> 00:00:25.399
do next.

7
00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:30.639
‘Practice one question before a conversation’ gives you somewhere to start.

8
00:00:30.639 --> 00:00:37.514
If that still feels too large, write the question down. Or say it privately

9
00:00:37.514 --> 00:00:38.005
first.

10
00:00:38.425 --> 00:00:44.776
Think of something you’ve been putting off. What would a smaller version look

11
00:00:44.776 --> 00:00:45.265
like?

12
00:00:45.265 --> 00:00:50.183
Opening the document instead of finishing the project. Practicing a greeting

13
00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:55.997
instead of planning a whole conversation. Asking a trusted person to help you

14
00:00:55.997 --> 00:00:56.444
prepare.

15
00:00:56.864 --> 00:01:00.804
Choose something safe, specific, and within your control.

16
00:01:00.804 --> 00:01:05.711
Afterward, notice what you attempted and what you learned. Feeling nervous

17
00:01:05.711 --> 00:01:07.496
doesn’t erase the effort.

18
00:01:07.496 --> 00:01:12.581
You can repeat the step, adjust it, or ask for support.

19
00:01:13.001 --> 00:01:19.470
Confidence doesn’t have to arrive all at once. Give yourself a chance to build

20
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.166
experience at a pace you can work with.
